    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_a77167b8",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image features a close-up of a man (identified as actor and comedian John Candy) holding a cigar, juxtaposed with text that reads: 'when you hear 'em yelling that allahakbar crap, just shoot 'em before they blow up a bomb, or start stabbin' and shootin' people.' This text directly targets individuals who identify as Muslim by associating them with terrorism, violence, and bomb threats. The meme uses the image of a seemingly benign, older white man to deliver a message that equates Muslim individuals with violent extremism, which is a harmful and hateful stereotype. The intent is to incite fear and hostility toward Muslims by promoting the dangerous and false notion that all Muslims are inherently violent or terrorist threats. This aligns with Islamophobic tropes that link Islam with barbarism and violence, and it is designed to provoke prejudice and potentially incite harm against Muslim communities.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_a38971b5"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
